From d3dd5373875c6af8b492a9c717bbddac91a9fdf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c-drew <101952850+c-drew@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 23:13:13 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] World prepare: stable chunk slots and change-tracked
 updates

Every frame the world prepare pass rebuilt the TLAS instance list and the geometry metadata
for all ~30k chunk slots, which cost up to ~4 ms of render-thread time while chunks stream in
(flying). Now each chunk slot owns a fixed metadata range (8 geometries per slot) and its TLAS
custom index is the slot number, so a frame only rewrites slots whose Chunks::slotSerials()
entry changed. SBT offsets come from one block per hit-group signature. The TLAS is built from
raw instances in a persistent buffer and refitted when the set of active slots is unchanged.

Metadata uploads are coalesced into copy regions with a 16 KB gap: after crossing a chunk
border ~800 slots relocate and the old per-slot copies (~2400 regions) cost 1-3 ms of GPU
time (rt.wp.copies p99 1.80 ms -> 0.16 ms).

Flying at 1440p, RTX 5090: 1% low 97-106 -> 140-151 fps; images identical.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
